      ],
      timeline: [
        '19th Century: German point-trick games diverge into Schafkopf (Bavaria) and Skat (Altenburg).',
        '1920s: Bauernstoss solidifies as the local tavern game of the Palatinate forest region.',
        'Present: Kept alive by local clubs and village tournaments, distinct from the standardized German Schafkopf Association rules.',
      ],
      evolution: "The name 'Bauernstoss' (Farmer's Push/Kick) likely refers to the aggressive nature of the bidding or the 'pushing' of points to the partner.",
