          deckDescription: 'One standard 32-card deck: eight ranks (seven through ace) in each of four suits. No jokers; used for Bauernstoss (Palatinate Schafkopf variant) where the four jacks are always the highest trumps and one suit is permanent trump.',
          suitDescription: 'Four French suits (hearts, diamonds, spades, clubs). One suit (usually hearts or diamonds) is permanent trump; the four jacks are the top trumps in jack order. Follow suit when able; point values apply for scoring.',
          rankDescription: 'Eight ranks per suit: ace (11 points), ten (10), king (4), queen (3), jack (2), nine and eight and seven (0). In trump the jacks are highest; then the trump suit cards in standard order. Point values are used for the team total.',
          dealPattern: 'Cards are dealt clockwise in two rounds of four cards each.',
